From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=EC=8B=AC=EC=83=81=EC=9B=90?= <dev.chamomile@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:34:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] tests: upstream unit tests on non-Linux hosts

Why: some upstream tests depend on Linux-only details that are not what
they test.

What: sockaddr_un without the Linux-only layout, host-specific ioctl
errors for /dev/null, NUL-padded peer paths, file metadata through each
host's extension trait, and tests that free one VM before creating the
next (Hypervisor.framework allows one VM per process).

Test: `cargo test -p vmm` on macOS; Linux results match upstream by test
name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
